--- body ---
## Context

The review-pr panel on PR #1143 ran two full five-seat rounds
(2026-10-02, Vibe runtime, `tools.agent.spawn` fan-out with the
`.md.part`-then-rename artifact contract). The docprop seat never produced a
report in either round.

Observable facts:

- Round 1: `agent.spawn` returned `{type: "success"}` for `r1143-docprop`.
  The subsequent `agent.list` polls showed only the other four seats
  (correctness, consistency, scope, redteam) — `r1143-docprop` was absent from
  the list entirely, while its four siblings appeared with live statuses.
- Round 2: same pattern for `r1143r2-docprop` — spawn success, no report, and
  the seat missing when listed.
- Both reviews degraded correctly by design (`PANEL-INTEGRITY: DEGRADED`,
  docprop named missing, `dissent: unavailable`) — the manifest check caught
  what the spawn result hid. But the root cause is a spawn that reports success
  for an agent that never exists.

Separately, in round 3 all four spawned seats vanished from `agent.list` after
the parent program's polling loop was interrupted (`client interrupt`) —
children do not survive an interrupted parent program. That behavior is
defensible; the silent-success spawn is not.

## Actions

1. Reproduce: spawn N agents in one program, poll `agent.list` immediately and
   after completion; find whether a success return can correspond to no agent.
2. If reproducible, make `agent.spawn` fail loudly (error result) when the
   agent cannot be created or listed, so the review-pr preflight
   ("a launch returns a depth-limit, permission, or other spawn error") can
   catch it — that preflight currently trusts the success return.
3. If not reproducible, record the runtime conditions of the two failures
   (Vibe unified harness, 2026-10-02, parallel five-seat panels) as a known
   intermittent.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Reproduction attempted with a written outcome
- [x] Spawn success implies the agent exists in `agent.list`, or the failure
      is documented as intermittent with the observed conditions
- [x] If a runtime-side fix is possible, the review-pr preflight note is
      updated to match what spawn results actually guarantee

Reproduction method committed at `scripts/repro-spawn-then-list.ts`
(top-level session artifact, not CI-wired). Written outcome in the log
(2026-10-03T12:10Z): NOT-REPRODUCED — silent-success documented as a known
intermittent with the observed conditions (PR #1143 rounds 1-2, 2026-10-02,
Vibe unified harness, five-seat parallel panels). No runtime-side fix is
possible from this repo (`agent.spawn` is Vibe CLI); the preflight note in
`skills/review-pr/SKILL.md` was updated regardless. Upstream issue filing is
an author decision.

## Test

- A scripted spawn-then-list check that fails when a success return has no
  corresponding agent entry.
